<title>SLOVENIA: Dolenjska to unite preferred shares.</title>
<headline>Dolenjska to unite preferred shares.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian bank Dolenjska Banka said on Thursday it would unite its preferred shares on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank said 7,965 preferred shares with a code will be joined with 70,778 preferred shares with a code.</p>
<p>The bank said it decided to weld the two together because both had the same characteristics apart from being issued at different dates.</p>
<p>The preferred shares represent 30 percent of the bank's equity. -- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
